---
title: Shakshuka
course: main
cuisine: middle-eastern
servings: 4
time_active: 15
time_total: 40
leftovers: poor
tags: [weeknight, one-pot]
description: Eggs poached in spiced tomato sauce.
---

Heat @olive oil{2%tbsp} in a #large skillet{} over medium. Sauté @onion{1}(diced) and @red bell pepper{1}(diced) until softened, ~{5%minutes}.

Add @garlic{3%clove}(minced) and cook until fragrant, ~{1%minutes}.

Stir in @cumin{2%tsp}, @paprika{2%tsp}, and @red pepper flakes{1%tsp}. Let the spices bloom, ~{30%seconds}.

Pour in @crushed tomatoes{1%can}(28 oz), season with @salt and @black pepper{}, and simmer until the sauce thickens slightly, ~{12%minutes}.

> A pinch of sugar can balance the acidity. A spoonful of harissa adds depth.

Make small wells in the sauce and crack @eggs{6} into them. Cover, reduce heat to medium-low, and cook until the whites are set but the yolks are still runny, ~{7%minutes}.

Top with @?feta cheese{}(crumbled) and @?cilantro{}(chopped). Serve straight from the skillet with crusty bread or pita for dipping.
